{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-457003-r4518969","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Mbongo Tchobi (Cameroonian Black Stew)","sourcePageId":457003,"sourceRevision":"4518969","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T17:19:33Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Mbongo%20Tchobi%20(Cameroonian%20Black%20Stew)&oldid=4518969","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:08:29.501Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Cameroonian recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"456cc5d5514455e104d7b4a657ba19072575096a2b56903bafffd5070eade9a1","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Stew recipes\n| Servings = 6\n| Time = 35 minutes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}{{Recipe}}\n__NOTOC__\n'''Mbongo tchobi''' is type of stew popular among the Bassa people of Cameroon, though it is also eaten in other countries. It can be eaten with rice and yam.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n* Large [[Cookbook:Fish|fish]] of choice, filleted\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 2 large (or 4 small) [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]], roughly [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* 1 large onion, chopped\n* 7 garlic cloves, peeled\n* ½ inch ginger root, peeled\n* ½ leek stem , chopped\n* ½ celery stalk, chopped\n* 2 seeds [[Cookbook:Calabash Nutmeg|African nutmeg]], peeled\n* 30 [[Cookbook:Njangsa|njangsa]] seeds\n* 4 teaspoons ground [[Cookbook:Alligator Pepper|mbongo spice]]\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|vegetable oil]]\n* ¼ teaspoon white [[Cookbook:Pepper|pepper]]\n* 1 habanero [[Cookbook:Chiles|chile pepper]] \n* 3 small [[Cookbook:Stock Cube|seasoning cubes]]\n\n== Equipment ==\n\n* Pot\n* [[Cookbook:Knife|Knife]]\n* [[Cookbook:Cutting Board|Cutting board]]\n* [[Cookbook:Cooktop|Stovetop]]\n* Cooking spoon\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n# Lightly salt the fish fillets, and set aside.\n# Combine the tomatoes, half the onions, garlic, ginger, leeks, celery, African nutmeg, njangsa, mbongo spice, and ½ cup water. [[Cookbook:Puréeing|Blend]] until smooth.\n# Pour the mixture over the fish, and [[Cookbook:Marinating|marinate]] for 30 minutes.\n# Heat the oil in a pot. Add the remaining onions and cook until aromatic. Add the fish, marinade, and peppers, then season with salt and stock cubes. Cover and cook for about 15 minutes.\n# Uncover and check the seasoning. Thin with water if necessary, then cook for another 5 minutes.\n# Serve with boiled plantains, rice, or yams.\n\n[[Category:Cameroonian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fish]]\n[[Category:Recipes for stew]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments]]\n[[Category:Recipes using akpi]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using habanero chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dehydrated broth]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fresh ginger]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using leek]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Mbongo Tchobi (Cameroonian Black Stew)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"6","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"Large fish of choice, filleted","sourceText":"Large fish of choice, filleted","amountText":"Large fish of choice, filleted","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null